.TH "ROARK\-METRIC\-DEFINITION\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-metric-definition-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-metric\-definition\-create \- Create custom metric definition
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark metric definition create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Create a new metric definition. The `calculationType` field selects the variant: LLM_JUDGE (LLM\-evaluated), FORMULA (computed from a math expression over other metrics), or PATTERN (detects a trigger→outcome pattern within a window). To create a threshold on top of an existing metric, use `POST /metric/definitions/{idOrSlug}/thresholds` instead.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/metric/definitions
.SH "REQUEST BODY"
This endpoint accepts one of several request shapes, so the body is supplied as JSON through \e\-\e\-data or on standard input rather than as individual flags.
.TP
\fBPromptMetricInput\fR
Requires calculationType, name, outputType.
.TP
\fBFormulaMetricInput\fR
Requires calculationType, name, outputType, formula, sources.
.TP
\fBPatternMetricInput\fR
Requires calculationType, name, operation, outcome.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
